@startuml

title The two directions of federation, and the one place the identity lives

left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor "a person" as person
actor "a client\n(an agent, or a tool)" as client

component "ores.http\n(the gateway:\ncookie, hardening,\nbrowser routes)" as gateway
component "ores.iam\n(providers, links,\nregistration, sessions,\nevents, grants)" as iam
component "the API\n(ores.http)" as api
cloud "an external\nidentity provider" as provider

person --> gateway : signs in
gateway --> provider : asks who this is
provider --> gateway : an issuer and a subject
gateway --> iam : sign in, or register the first time

client --> gateway : asks to act for a person
gateway --> person : asks for consent
gateway --> iam : writes the grant the consent names
client --> api : calls, with a token IAM minted
iam --> api : the keys that verify it

note right of iam
  Both directions end in the same place. The provider's
  answer becomes a link, and a client's consent becomes
  a grant, so the audit, the revocation and the second
  person who may approve are the same ones either way.
end note

@enduml
